## Bug

`memory_search` with `threshold: 0` returns `{ results: [], total: 0 }` even when there are stored entries with embeddings that match the query.

## Reproduction

```js
// Step 1: store an entry
await memory_store({
  namespace: "search-repro",
  key: "smoke",
  value: "the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"
});
// → { success: true, hasEmbedding: true, embeddingDimensions: 384 }

// Step 2: search with threshold 0 (intent: "show me everything")
await memory_search({
  namespace: "search-repro",
  query: "quick brown fox",
  threshold: 0
});
// Expected: 1 result with positive similarity
// Actual:   { results: [], total: 0 }

// Step 3: same call with threshold 0.001 — works
await memory_search({
  namespace: "search-repro",
  query: "quick brown fox",
  threshold: 0.001
});
// → { results: [{ key: "smoke", similarity: 0.6998 }], total: 1 }
```

## Root cause

`dist/src/mcp-tools/memory-tools.js:298`:

```js
const threshold = input.threshold || 0.3;
```

The `||` operator coerces falsy values, so `threshold: 0` is silently substituted with the default `0.3`. The user's explicit `0` never reaches `searchEntries`. Same anti-pattern as #1489 (which fixed `namespace || 'default'`), different parameter.

## Suggested fix

```diff
-            const threshold = input.threshold || 0.3;
+            const threshold = input.threshold ?? 0.3;
```

Verified locally on v3.5.80: this single line restores documented behavior.

## Sibling occurrences (audit)

Same `||` numeric-default anti-pattern in 6 other handlers (would similarly drop a user-supplied `0`):

- `mcp-tools/agent-tools.js:480` — `threshold || 0.5`
