## Bug 1 — `ruflo status` (and other one-shot commands) hang ~2 min before exit

Any one-shot command prints its output correctly, then the process fails to exit for ~2 minutes. Affects both `ruflo status` and `ruflo --version` (less noticeable on the latter because the output is tiny).

Root cause is in `ruflo/bin/ruflo.js`. The wrapper only has `.catch()` on `cli.run()`:

```js
cli.run().catch((error) => {
  console.error('Fatal error:', error.message);
  process.exit(1);
});
```

No explicit `process.exit(0)` on success. Node relies on the event loop draining, but `@claude-flow/cli` leaves a handle open somewhere, so the process hangs.

The canonical `@claude-flow/cli/bin/cli.js` already handles this with a comment citing issue #1552:

```js
cli.run()
  .then(() => {
    // #1552: Exit cleanly after one-shot commands.
    process.exit(0);
  })
  .catch((error) => { ... });
```

The ruflo wrapper just didn't copy the `.then()` branch.

## Bug 2 — `[AgentDB Patch] Controller index not found` warning leaks on every invocation

The canonical `@claude-flow/cli/bin/cli.js` patches `console.warn` to drop these messages:

```js
console.warn = (...args) => {
  const msg = String(args[0] ?? '');
  if (msg.includes('[AgentDB Patch]')) return;
  _origWarn.apply(console, args);
};
```

The ruflo wrapper imports `dist/src/index.js` directly, bypassing this shim, so the warning prints on every command — even `ruflo --version`.

