## TL;DR

`killStaleDaemons()` in `daemon.js` greps all `ps` output for `daemon start --foreground` and SIGTERMs them, **without filtering by `projectRoot`**. The function's `projectRoot` parameter is only used to fetch `trackedPid` for self-protection. As a result, **every `daemon start` invocation kills daemons in every other workspace on the same machine**.

This contradicts ADR-014's design intent ("Daemon state is persisted to `.claude-flow/daemon-state.json` within project directories") and breaks operators running multiple parallel Claude Code workspaces.

## Repro

```bash
# Workspace A
cd ~/workspace-A && npx claude-flow@alpha daemon start  # PID 100

# Workspace B
cd ~/workspace-B && npx claude-flow@alpha daemon start  # PID 200, kills PID 100 via killStaleDaemons

# Result: PID 100 dead, only PID 200 alive
```

Verified on macOS arm64, Node 25, ruflo v3.7.0-alpha.20 (claude-flow v3.6.30 path).

## Source (`v3/@claude-flow/cli/dist/src/commands/daemon.js`)

```js
async function killStaleDaemonsPosix(projectRoot, quiet) {
    // ...
    const psOutput = execFileSync('ps', ['-eo', 'pid,command'], ...);
    const lines = psOutput.split('\n');
    const currentPid = process.pid;
    const trackedPid = getBackgroundDaemonPid(projectRoot);  // ← only used as self-exemption
    for (const line of lines) {
        if (!line.includes('daemon start --foreground')) continue;
        if (!line.includes('claude-flow') && !line.includes('@claude-flow/cli')) continue;
        const pidStr = line.trim().split(/\s+/)[0];
        const pid = parseInt(pidStr, 10);
        if (isNaN(pid) || pid === currentPid || pid === trackedPid) continue;
        if (!isProcessRunning(pid)) continue;
        // ← NO check that the killed PID belongs to projectRoot
        process.kill(pid, 'SIGTERM');
    }
}
```

The intent of `killStaleDaemons` is to fix zombie accumulation (#1551). That fix should kill stale daemons IN THE CURRENT WORKSPACE, not all workspaces system-wide.

## ADR-014 contradiction

ADR-014 (`v3/implementation/adrs/ADR-014-workers-system.md`) states the daemon is **project-scoped**: state, metrics, logs all live in `<projectRoot>/.claude-flow/`. The kill behavior contradicts that scope.

## Impact

Operators running multiple Claude Code workspaces in parallel (typical for monorepo / multi-project / multi-Nexus setups, e.g., 60 BladeRunner-style workspaces) can only have ONE daemon alive at a time. Every new `daemon start` cascade-kills the others. Result:

- Only the most-recently-started workspace has autopilot workers (audit/optimize/consolidate/map/testgaps) running
- AgentDB only populates in the currently-active workspace
- Workers in other workspaces silently die mid-run

## Suggested fix

Filter the kill loop by `projectRoot`. Two approaches:

### Option A: parse cwd from ps `-eo pid,command,wd` (POSIX-portable subset)

```js
const psOutput = execFileSync('ps', ['-eo', 'pid,wd,command'], ...);
// ...
for (const line of lines) {
    const m = line.match(/^\s*(\d+)\s+(\S+)\s+(.*)$/);
    if (!m) continue;
    const [_, pidStr, cwd, cmd] = m;
    if (!cmd.includes('daemon start --foreground')) continue;
    if (cwd !== projectRoot) continue;  // ← scope filter
    // ...kill...
}
```

Caveat: `wd` column not POSIX-standard, varies per OS (`ps -eo lstart` etc.).

### Option B: each daemon writes a sentinel file with its projectRoot, kill only by matching

Daemon on startup writes `~/.ruflo/daemon-registry/<pid>.json` with `{projectRoot, pid, startedAt}`. `killStaleDaemons` reads registry, filters by `projectRoot`, kills only those.

Both options preserve the #1551 zombie fix while respecting ADR-014 scoping.

### Option C (alternate): make killStale opt-in via flag

Default to NO global kill. Operator who wants the legacy behavior passes `--kill-stale-global`. Multi-workspace operators get sane behavior by default.

## Workaround (until fix)

For multi-workspace operators, only the most-recently-started daemon survives. Either:
- Don't auto-start daemons (`autoStart: false`); manual `daemon start` in the active workspace only
- Patch local ruflo source to no-op `killStaleDaemons`

